<h1>VNotes engineering manual</h1>
<p>A task is either active or completed. A voice take becomes durable text when recognition finishes. The application runs on Android 8 or later and uses English Moonshine Tiny on the device. Network access supplies the initial model download.</p>
<h2>Reading and changing the program</h2>
<p>Read the chapters in order for the interaction model, the Flutter-to-Android boundary, audio processing, storage, and the build. Each file root names a destination relative to <code>code/</code>. Named chunks inside a root expand in the displayed order. Edit the corresponding chapter in <code>src/</code>, then run <code>python3 scripts/literate.py</code>. The script invokes notangle for each file and noweave for this cross-referenced manual. Its <code>--check</code> mode detects drift between either generated output and the sources.</p>
<h2>Ownership and boundaries</h2>
<p>Dart owns widget state, user decisions, and Material 3 presentation. Android owns the microphone permission, audio hardware, model files, document picker and SQLite transactions. A method channel carries commands, text and meter readings. Keeping PCM and inference on the Android side avoids copying a continuous audio stream through the Flutter engine. The Kotlin components for capture and persistence carry forward the existing file formats and model directory.</p>
<p>For a typed task, the composer trims the input, calls add, then reloads the committed list. For a recording, the capture thread feeds the serial recognition worker, which publishes revisable hypotheses. At stop, capture writes retry audio before the worker flushes its final hypothesis. A new task uses the stable take ID. A recorded replacement goes through an editable review dialog.</p>
